1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,597
Fast aircraft and drones.

2
00:00:05,697 --> 00:00:10,640
A collision, an engine failure, a flash that blinds every camera.

3
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:13,763
When the view is lost, what should the screen say?

4
00:00:14,613 --> 00:00:17,999
MoVi declares what it has not observed.

5
00:00:18,099 --> 00:00:20,205
Three answers per track.

6
00:00:20,305 --> 00:00:21,601
I see it.

7
00:00:21,701 --> 00:00:24,724
I don't see it, but here is where it can be.

8
00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:26,397
Or: I don't know.

9
00:00:27,447 --> 00:00:31,643
An aircraft on approach, and a drone that broadcasts nothing.

10
00:00:31,743 --> 00:00:38,564
In six flight scenarios, MoVi never said clear where an aircraft, a drone or a fragment was.

11
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:44,208
An engine fails at a hundred and thirty-five metres per second.

12
00:00:44,308 --> 00:00:46,307
A flash, then smoke.

13
00:00:46,407 --> 00:00:55,724
MoVi infers the event and declares both cameras unreliable within three cycles, in sixty of sixty simulated runs.

14
00:00:55,824 --> 00:01:01,493
Low-energy debris stays inside the declared volume in fifty-eight of sixty.

15
00:01:02,343 --> 00:01:06,710
Two drones close at forty and thirty-five metres per second.

16
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:11,071
MoVi warns of the close pass at least ten seconds ahead.

17
00:01:11,171 --> 00:01:21,127
After the impact, the collision is not yet recognised as an event, but the region is kept: in every simulated run, the fragments stayed inside it.

18
00:01:21,977 --> 00:01:26,323
A flash blinds every optical sensor for three seconds.

19
00:01:26,423 --> 00:01:29,980
Radar alone keeps a region for every track.

20
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:33,341
Now continuity is lost.

21
00:01:33,441 --> 00:01:38,577
In the motion model, the confidence is computed exactly, in closed form.

22
00:01:38,677 --> 00:01:44,495
A fixed zone loses it in seconds, so the region grows to keep nine chances in ten.

23
00:01:44,595 --> 00:01:54,530
On sixteen real aircraft tracks, with a simulated sensor, it held them ninety-two to ninety-eight times in a hundred, from three to thirty seconds.

24
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:59,040
At one to two seconds, only seventy-one: a declared limit.

25
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:02,268
Dedicated hardware?

26
00:02:02,368 --> 00:02:11,685
Chips built for one job, like those now serving language models, suggest processing in about a millisecond: an estimate by analogy.

27
00:02:11,785 --> 00:02:15,469
The sensor's revisit still dominates the delay.

28
00:02:16,519 --> 00:02:23,895
The same core works on a site: a drone behind a building, warned in time in two hundred of two hundred runs.

29
00:02:23,995 --> 00:02:27,295
And at short range: people, cars, trains.

30
00:02:28,345 --> 00:02:29,577
The limits.

31
00:02:29,677 --> 00:02:35,623
Everything is simulated, with no physical sensor, and classes are labelled by hand.

32
00:02:35,723 --> 00:02:45,359
From prototype to deployed system: a contact rule for fast collisions, state-of-the-art sensors, dedicated hardware, field trials.

33
00:02:45,459 --> 00:02:46,712
MoVi.

34
00:02:46,812 --> 00:02:49,131
It observes and warns.

35
00:02:49,231 --> 00:02:50,953
By SDMs.

